---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_65",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 65,
  "text": "[[162.1]] <b>53.  Tentamina de definitione quantitatis [März bis April 1679 (?)]</b>\n [[162.2]] <tab/>[März bis April 1679 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[162.8]] Forma sive qualitas in toto pariter et in parte observatur. At quantitas et figura non\n[[162.9]] perinde in toto et in parte. </p>\n<p> [[162.10]] Hujusmodi forma est ipsa extensio, itemque cogitatio. </p>\n<p> [[162.11]] Motus non est aliqua forma, neque est Ens quoddam, neque enim unquam verum est\n[[162.12]] aliquid moveri, nisi per aggregatum multorum temporum in unum; est ergo ens per\n[[162.13]] accidens seu per aggregationem. Eodem modo patet nec tempus Ens esse, sed Entia\n[[162.14]] quibus unum impositum nomen. </p>\n<p> [[162.15]] Quantitas est ex earum rerum numero quae absolutam veramque realitatem non\n[[162.16]] habent. Nam si universa quae sunt in mundo duplo majora esse fingerentur, eadem\n[[162.17]] proportione nulla sentiretur mutatio ne a Deo quidem. </p>\n<p> [[162.18]] Quantitas non potest distincte concipi nec ullam habet notam qua retineri ac internosci\n[[162.19]] possit. Itaque qui quantitatem aliquam retinere capit, extrinseca aliqua re indiget,\n[[162.20]] quam semper secum ferat, et ad quam id de cujus quantitate agitur exploret. </p>\n<p> [[162.21]] Hinc apparet duas res caetera similes, quae sola quantitate differant non posse\n[[162.22]] distingui, nisi vel ope alicujus externae notae quam circumgestamus, et ad [quam] rem\n[[162.23]] applicamus, vel saltem per compraesentiam; nam cum simul videmus ambo, tunc non\n[[162.24]] difficulter res distinguimus; altera enim erga alteram velut mensura est. </p>\n<p> [[162.25]] Quantitas non est eadem in toto ac in partibus est tamen aliquid simile in toto ac in\n[[162.26]] partibus. </p>\n<p> [[162.27]] Quantitas servit ad inveniendas omnes partes rei itaque quantitas est quodammodo\n[[162.28]] rei totalitas. </p>\n<p> [[163.1]] Quantitas est enumeratio partium rei aliunde certarum seu definitae quantitatis. Quae\n[[163.2]] si sint aequales, erit quantitas numerus partium; ipse numerus est aliqua quantitas, nam\n[[163.3]] nisi numeralia nomina haberentur nemo discernere posset 12 a 11. Externo igitur aliquo\n[[163.4]] auxilio opus est, quod cum ipso numero nullam realem habet connexionem. </p>\n<p> [[163.5]] Quantitas est omnium rei partium expressio. </p>\n<p> [[163.6]] Quantitas est quod ad idem aliquid in parte eandem habet relationem quam habet\n[[163.7]] totum ad partem. Seu si sit <i>a</i> in toto, et <i>b</i> in parte, et in omni parte sit <i>a</i> ad <i>b</i>, ut totum ad\n[[163.8]] eam partem, discerni non possit comparatio. </p>\n<p> [[163.9]] Quantitas exhibet modum cognoscendi quaenam sint rei partes, quantitas praebet\n[[163.10]] modum inveniendi rei terminos, et quid sit intra aut extra ipsam; non consideratis formis\n[[163.11]] seu qualitatibus. </p>\n<p> [[163.12]] Quantitas est possibilitas congruendi cum re certa, congruere autem intelligo non\n[[163.13]] aequalia tantum, sed et inaequalia repetitione. </p>\n<p> [[163.14]] Ratio est duarum rerum congruendi possibilitas itaque quantitas est rationis species. <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: Cum in ratione non discernitur utrum mensura vel mensuratum non potest aestimari nisi per logarithmos, ut in Musica.</Fn>\n[[163.15]] Caeterum hac definitione continentur et rationes ineffabiles seu quae numeris exprimi\n[[163.16]] non possunt, nisi certa progressionis in infinitum specie. </p>\n<p> [[163.17]] Congruere est quoad omnes partes aeque similiter positum\n[[163.18]] esse, ita <i>ABCD</i> et <i>abcd</i> non sunt quoad omnes partes aeque similiter\n[[163.19]] posita patet enim partem <i>D</i> esse utrique communem at <i>A</i> ab <i>a</i>\n[[163.20]] distare et magis distare <i>B</i> a <i>b</i> quam <i>A</i> ab <i>a</i>. Sed si congruunt omnia\n[[163.21]] nullum tale discrimen notari potest, <Fn><i>Am Rande</i>: Ex hac definitione sequitur congruere etiam quae non sunt in eodem loco, exempli causa duo plana similia aequalia, et sibi regione posita, ita ut puncta respondentia aequidistent.</Fn> nolui autem definire congruentiam\n[[163.22]] per locum, ut congrua sint, quae sunt in eodem loco, quia etiam tempora et\n[[164.1]] motus et rationes et numeri, et omnia quae positionem habent, [congruere possunt.]\n[[164.2]] Positio est ultimum discrimen quo discerni possunt, etiam quae per omnia similia sunt\n[[164.3]] quae in ipsis percipi intelligive possunt. Estque relatio quaedam ad alias res quoad\n[[164.4]] existentiam, seu rerum coexistentia, nam et quae eodem momento non existunt, tamen\n[[164.5]] coexistunt, saltem enim existunt in eodem anno vel seculo. Idem est de loco. </p>\n<p> [[164.6]] Si definias quantitatem modum quo quid cum alia re congruere potest, erunt ejusdem\n[[164.7]] rei diversae quantitates nam diversis modis fieri potest ut eadem res cum alia\n[[164.8]] congruat. Nisi respondeamus resolutione facta in id quod commune est alterum in altero\n[[164.9]] contineri. Quanquam in incommensurabilibus haec resolutio locum non habeat. </p>\n<p> [[164.10]] Nec videtur quantitas esse possibilitas congruendi, nam possibilitas congruendi est\n[[164.11]] communis omnibus quae sunt ejusdem generis. </p>\n<p> [[164.12]] An ergo dicemus? Quantitas est designatio [seu] determinatio omnium rei partium\n[[164.13]] secundum possibilitatem congruendi cum rebus certis. Vel quia aliud quantitas aliud\n[[164.14]] designatio seu expressio quantitatis erit possibilitas congruendi cum rebus certis, qua\n[[164.15]] totum a qualibet parte aut eo quod cum parte ejus congruit distinguitur. </p>\n<p> [[164.16]] Hinc video jam et posse quantitatem definiri sine assumtione rei certae extrinsecae.\n[[164.17]] Imo non licet, nam non sciemus absolute rei quantitatem nisi alio assumto. </p>\n<p> [[164.18]] Quantitas est possibilitas congruendi cum re certa vel rebus certis distinguens totum\n[[164.19]] a parte quacunque. </p>\n<p> [[164.20]] Addidi vel rebus certis, quia quantitas rei definita est, si omnes ejus partes congruant\n[[164.21]] rebus certis, sed aliae aliis ut si partem reperias congruere diagonali quadrati certi ex\n[[164.22]] orichalco formati; alteram partem lateri. </p>\n<p> [[164.23]] Certam rem intelligo, quam in individuo habemus, et quoad id de quo agitur id est\n[[164.24]] quoad congruendi potentiam nullam mutationem subiisse scimus, ut regula ex orichalco. </p>\n",
  "number": "53.",
  "title": "Tentamina de definitione quantitatis",
  "date": "[März bis April 1679 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:53. Tentamina de definitione quantitatis [März bis April 1679 (?)] [März bis April 1679 (?)] Forma sive qualitas in toto pariter et in parte observatur. At quantitas et figura non perinde in toto et in parte. Hujusmodi forma est ipsa extensio, itemque cogitatio. Motus non est aliqua forma, neque est...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>